    "chunk_text": "and who consequently had, as at the dayimmediately preceding the date of the cominginto operation of this Act, been unable to complywith the requirements of paragraph (a) of section2, shall, if such person satisfies the requirementsof paragraphs (b) and (c) of that section or isable to submit proof that such person is a\n\nShort title.\n\n\u201cGrant ofCitizenship tocertainpersons.\n\nInsertion ofsection 2A in Act,No. 39 of 1988.\n\nGrant of Citizenship to Stateless Persons(Special Provisions) (Amendment)Act, No. 5 of 2009\n\n2\n\ndescendant of a person who was a permanentresident of Sri Lanka with Indian Origin, havethe status of a citizen of Sri Lanka with effectfrom the date of commencement of this Act andshall be entitled to all the rights and privilegesto which a citizens of Sri Lanka is entitled to bylaw.\u201d.\n\n3.Section 4 of the principal enactment is herebyamended in subsection (1) thereof\u2014\n\n(1)by the substitution for the words and figures \u201cbyreason of the provisions of section 2\u201d, of the wordsand figures \u201cby reason of the provisions of section2 or 2A\u201d; and\n\n(2)by the substitution for the words \u201csubstantially inthe Form set out in Schedule B to this Act.\u201d, of thewords and figures \u201csubstantially in the Form setout in Schedule B to this Act:\n\nProvided however, any person who is entitled tothe status of a citizen of Sri Lanka under theprovision of section 2A, shall apply for a Certificateof Citizenship under this Act, only upon his arrivalin Sri Lanka with the intention of permanentlyresiding in Sri Lanka.\u201d.\n\n4.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand the Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendment ofsection 4 of theprincipalenactment.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\n3Grant of Citizenship to Stateless Persons(Special Provisions) (Amendment)Act, No. 5 of 2009"
